WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.010
Where did you get that?

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:06.180
It's a short question, and it can ruin a very beautiful report.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:12.060
Because you typed a question into a chat, and a confident, well-written answer came back.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.310
But you don't know which sources it used, or what it left out.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.310
It's like getting into a taxi and saying, somewhere good, please.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.610
You get a very smooth ride,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:23.880
to somewhere.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.560
That's because the search started before the thinking.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.740
Good research starts with a precise question, clear limits and a plan for where to look.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:39.680
Then you check the result, because AI sometimes cites a page that doesn't support the claim.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:45.900
So, in this adventure, you do this on one real question from your work, and save the method.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:51.160
By the end, you can answer in two sentences, and name the source behind each.
